Article 2 For the purpose of these Measures, cable television refers to the following public television transmission systems that use cables or optical cables to transmit television programs:
(1) cable television stations that receive and transmit wireless television programs and broadcast self-produced television programs and video tapes;
(2) cable television stations that receive and transmit wireless television programs and broadcast video tapes;
(3) shared antenna systems that receive and transmit wireless television programs.

Article 4 Any State organ, military unit, organization, enterprise, or institution that meets the following conditions may apply to establish a cable television station:
(1) conforming to the overall planning requirements of the local television coverage network;
(2) having a specialized administrative body, and full-time personnel for interviewing, editing, production, camera operation, broadcasting, transmission, and technical maintenance;
(3) having reliable sources of funds;
(4) having camera, editing, and broadcasting equipment certified as conforming to the relevant national technical standards by the administrative department of radio and television at or above the provincial level;
(5) having a fixed program production site;
(6) having transmission equipment certified as conforming to the relevant national technical standards by the administrative department of radio and television at or above the provincial level;
(7) having a fixed broadcasting site.
Any entity that meets the conditions specified in items (1), (3), (6), and (7) of the preceding paragraph may apply to establish a cable television station.
It is prohibited to use a cable television station to broadcast self-produced television programs.
An individual shall not apply to establish a cable television station.

Article 15 The local administrative departments of radio and television at or above the county level shall be responsible for supervising and inspecting local cable television facilities and cable television broadcasting activities, and may, depending on the seriousness of the circumstances, impose corresponding administrative penalties for acts violating these Measures:
(1) For a cable television station that violates the provisions of Article 8, Article 9, Article 10, or Article 11 of these Measures, a warning, a fine of not more than 20,000 yuan, or revocation of the license may be imposed, and it may be recommended that the unit to which the directly responsible person belongs shall impose administrative sanctions on the person;
(2) For a person who, without obtaining a license, privately establishes a cable television station in violation of Article 6 of these Measures, who privately uses a cable television station to broadcast self-produced television programs in violation of Article 4 of these Measures, or who privately uses a shared antenna system to broadcast self-produced television programs or video tapes in violation of Article 5 of these Measures, a warning or a fine of not more than 20,000 yuan may be imposed, and the broadcasting equipment may be confiscated at the same time;
(3) For a person who, without obtaining the Design (Installation) License for Cable Television Station or for Cable Television Station and Shared Antenna System, privately undertakes the design or installation tasks of a cable television station or a shared antenna system in violation of Article 7 of these Measures, in addition to being ordered to cease the illegal business activities, a fine of not more than 10,000 yuan may be imposed.
